The rule tables, the classification semantics and the ordering inside
`decide()` in `src/permgate/domain/` are ported from **CoreCoder**, an
open-source teaching project, which is also MIT licensed:

    MIT License
    Copyright (c) 2026 Yufeng He
    https://github.com/he-yufeng/CoreCoder

That copyright notice and permission notice are reproduced in full above (the
same MIT text, which the licence requires be retained) and the provenance of
each ported artefact is recorded in `README.md` §10. The conformance fixture in
`tests/fixtures/conformance.tsv` deliberately freezes the reference
implementation's output for 119 commands so that the port can be verified
rather than asserted.
